# Single Source of Truth for Defaults and Constants

When a default value, magic number, or configuration constant appears in more than one place, extract it to a single definition and reference it everywhere.

- C#: use a `static` factory method, `const`, or `static readonly` field on the most relevant type.
- JS/TS: define a `const` at the top of the module; never repeat literals in multiple functions.
- Never duplicate the same literal in both a property initializer and a normalization/migration method — point both at the same definition.
